From: ksre-ps5
Subject: timemodule: reject a format ending in a bare %E/%O on the PS5

The console libc's wcsftime() does not return when the format string ends in
the modifier "%E" or "%O" with no conversion character (console evidence:
test_time.test_strftime_invalid_format hung on ' %E'; ' %O' likewise; every
other ' %<char>' and "%Ec", "%Od", "%E ", ... return normally). Raise
ValueError("Invalid format string") for that case instead, as CPython does
on other platforms with invalid formats. Only compiled for __PROSPERO__.

SPDX-License-Identifier: PSF-2.0
--- a/Modules/timemodule.c	2026-11-10 09:14:28
+++ b/Modules/timemodule.c	2026-11-10 09:14:28
@@ -832,6 +832,19 @@
         }
     }
 #endif
+#if defined(__PROSPERO__) && defined(HAVE_WCSFTIME)
+    /* PS5: the console libc's wcsftime() never returns when the format ends in
+       the bare modifier "%E" or "%O" (console evidence, 03b). Reject it the
+       way other platforms reject an invalid format. */
+    for (const time_char *f = wcschr(format, '%'); f != NULL; f = wcschr(f + 2, '%')) {
+        if (f[1] == L'\0')
+            break;
+        if ((f[1] == L'E' || f[1] == L'O') && f[2] == L'\0') {
+            PyErr_SetString(PyExc_ValueError, "Invalid format string");
+            return NULL;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
 
